    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d627-a1">

                <pb facs="1018" n="882" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg882"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    155.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. St. Victor to Mr.
                            Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State, Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1887-11-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 17, 1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I have had the honor of receiving
                    your two communications dated the 12th instant, relative to the interest and the
                    bonds of the Caisse d’Aniortissement that your legation hold for the account of
                    American citizens.</p>
                <p>I hastened to communicate to the council of ministers the contents of those two
                    dispatches, and I have the honor to inform you that the Government has decided
                    that my honorable colleague, the secretary of state of finances, will have a
                    personal understanding with your legation for the regulation of the two
                    questions to which you have had the kindness to call my attention.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">B. St.
                        Victor.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
